  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SFD-My Daughter</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sisterhood founded by Hmong ethnic women who concern of ethnic women&apos;s education and economic. First two grants received from Voice(2018-2019 and 2020-2021) focus on staff&#x2019;s capacity building and empowerment ethnic minority youth accessed education and employment. This project aims to ship from ethnic youth who completed our women empowerment program to their community in rural area in province where they came from. 40 women from our previous program will be identify and select as ethnic role model who stand for girls and women education to implementing community dialogues on our daughter&#x2019;s education and youth mentorship activity in community with early school drop out of girls and women.

Overall goal: Communities attitude change on support women andgirls to education and socialservice.
Objective:
1. To strengthen transformative leadership of 40 role model who completed our empowerment program to build their confidence and skills through their outreach activities planning;
2. To created space forwomen role model and community discussionabout women&#x2019;s successful and community strategy for keep their daughter in school;
3. To forge alliances with National Lao Front toinitiative strategy of addressing gender base violence and early school dropout.</narrative>
  </description>
